# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and NO backtick (set -u in the runner).
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_coverage_185.py" "EXTRACTOR-COVERAGE GATE: PASS" "extractor coverage: TS exported-const + class-field-arrow symbols, TS/Go cross-tier request URLs, Go nested route-group prefixes" "extractor coverage from the root (audit-driven, 11-repo read-only 实测): (1) an exported const bound to a NON-function value (store factory defineStore, Zod/Yup validator z.object, config/lookup map, singleton) now mints a first-class def symbol -- the #1 TypeScript-market gap (measured miss directus 57pct, NestJS 86pct, tRPC 90pct, plane 94pct) -- PRECISION-SCOPED to DIRECTLY-EXPORTED top-level bindings (a bare local const, or a const re-exported only via export-clause, mints NOTHING); (2) class-field ARROW methods (the MobX/Angular fetch = async arrow idiom, a public_field_definition not a method_definition) now mint a def (plane_web 490 such, 0 before), with plain DATA fields minting nothing; (3) the within-repo request matcher now recognizes this.get/post/put/patch/delete(url) wrapper-method requests (plane_web 340, 0 before); (4) Go client/SDK request URLs (getResponse/getParsedResponse with a string or Sprintf format URL, percent-verbs collapsed to a template token) now extract on the CONSUMER side (go-sdk repo.go 0 of 10 before -> all captured), with a pure-backend Go file issuing nothing and a Go SDK client defining nothing (clean definer/consumer split); (5) Go NESTED route-group prefixes (gin RouterGroup / chi Route / echo Group closure mounting m.Group prefix func) are joined via a brace-depth scanner like the Python/NestJS prefix paths, not left as bare leaf segments. Mints kind def only (the schema node_kind CHECK set -- a const/binding kind would be silently dropped at ingest and need a DDL migration). 28 checks: every recall assertion paired with a precision floor; hermetic, content-free (symbol names + normalized URL paths only)." "extractor coverage from the root: the audit's top-5 missed-symbol/missed-route patterns -- exported non-function consts, class-field arrow methods, this.verb request calls, Go client request URLs, Go nested route-group prefixes -- are captured on fixtures WITH a precision floor (no junk minted: a non-exported local const, a plain data field, a Go client mis-read as a route definer, a pure backend mis-read as a requester all stay empty). RECALL up, PRECISION not down; kind def only so NO schema change. Gate 185." 18
